Two backports onto @anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime 0.0.79. Drop each part when a
released version carries it, and the whole patch (and the patchedDependencies
entry in package.json) when both are released and Ave pins that version.
test/scripts/asrt-patched-symbols.test.ts fails if either part is missing from
the installed package.

1. https://github.com/anthropics/sandbox-runtime/pull/722 (issue #721): a
   per-wrap `ttys` option that grants file-ioctl on the named pty slave only,
   so the workspace terminal's shell can set its own tty (no double echo,
   working job control) without allowPty's grant on every /dev/ttys*.

2. Attribution for the ask callback: `SandboxAskCallback` receives a second
   argument `{ attributionKey }`, the decoded proxy-username key (the
   wrap's `commandId`) that the same function already hands
   `recordOutboundDeny`. Without it an embedder that runs several
   invocations through the one process-wide proxy cannot tell which of them
   opened the connection it is asked about. Prepared for upstream as
   "pass the attribution key to SandboxAskCallback".

